#: R/decisioncombine.b.R
msgid ""
"PPV and NPV depend on prevalence, so they transfer to another population "
"only if its disease rate is similar. Sensitivity, specificity and the "
"likelihood ratios are less prevalence-dependent, though not independent of "
"it. LR+ and LR- are the more useful numbers to carry elsewhere not because "
"they are more stable -- being functions of sensitivity and specificity, they "
"inherit exactly the same dependence -- but because they convert a pre-test "
"probability into a post-test probability at whatever prevalence the new "
"setting has."
